    "workspacePlansOwnersVerbatim": true,
    "arithmetic": "Two independently exact integer byte rows share Q30 widening/replication only. Original four-tap disjoint subsets/reduction and tail remain per row, bounded<2^47 RGB/<2^39 alpha. Exact whole-row Double conversion, all Q30/error/Guard/certificates/repair and ordered vertical FMA unchanged. No broader numerical policy.",
    "scheduling": "One scheduler source has closed single/pair modes selected once at entry: byte fast vertical reduction can batch two immediate actual missing nonzero tap rows when slots>1. All other cases erase batching state/calls and retain measured single kernels. Keep two useful row schedules rather than impose unused span arguments or inlined-helper register pressure on original single-row loop. Final actual code proves original byte668B and word1003B instructions unchanged; single scheduler1633B erases pair calls, pair2575B uses977B producer. Code sizes alone not CPU evidence.",
    "lifetime": "Same two existing distinct modulo cache slots, publish IDs only after both rows/conversions complete. No unused rows, added capacity, arrays, retained weight vectors, sessions, pool, owner or root. Existing borrowed input/plan/root, result admission, cleanup and cancellation; failed private work abandoned and next operation resets all row IDs.",
    "scope": "Shared scheduler and byte paired preparation change; all8 existing complete boundaries refresh. Five existing row cases extend to two distinct rows with BigInteger bit exactness/guards/source/noallocation/root; no new test count, benchmark shape, reference or quality setting. Three successful coherent main/embedded versions/OS; all intermediate adverse evidence retained.",
